{% comment %}
  Prince Tires — Seasonal Planes Hero (pt-hero-season-planes)

  One hero. The layered artwork of pt-cinema-planes driven by the five-state
  date logic of pt-hero-seasonal, so the scene itself changes with Calgary's
  calendar rather than just the words on top of it.

  Layer order (back -> front):
     0  backdrop plate(s)      slow crossfade if more than one is set
     1  far road plate         summer or winter surface, picked by season
     2  snow — far plane       winter states only, pure CSS
     3  tire cut-outs          4 planes, own scale/brightness/depth
     4  snow — near plane      falls in FRONT of the far tires
     5  front road plate       the tires sit *in* the scene, not on it
     6  directional scrim      legibility on the copy side only
     7  season glow            red in winter, orange in spring/summer
     8  content                eyebrow, H1, subhead, search, CTAs
     9  vignette

  Everything that decides the state runs in Liquid, so only the active season's
  images are ever requested and a crawler reads the live message as real text.
  assets/pt-weather.js is optional on top: it fills in the live Calgary
  temperature and boosts the snow when it is genuinely snowing. The hero is
  complete and correct without it.

  Windows (auto mode, by MMDD) — same as pt-hero-seasonal so the two agree:
    preseason    Sep 1  - Oct 10
    changeover   Oct 11 - Nov 30
    deep_winter  Dec 1  - Mar 10
    spring       Mar 11 - Apr 30
    summer       May 1  - Aug 31

  The search is snippets/pt-smart-search - the same single-input search the
  old hero-smart-search section shipped, extracted so it can live in any hero.

  Every image setting is optional: left blank, the layer resolves the matching
  pt-cine-*.png from Settings -> Files via the file_url filter, so the section
  renders the full scene the moment it is added. The pickers are overrides.

  Never write alignment, tire storage, or mobile service into any state —
  Prince Tires does not offer them. Never suggest a size other than the
  vehicle's stock size.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign mmdd = 'now' | date: '%m%d' | times: 1
  assign mode = section.settings.season_mode | default: 'auto'

  if mode == 'auto'
    assign active_key = 'summer'
    if mmdd >= 901 and mmdd <= 1010
      assign active_key = 'preseason'
    elsif mmdd >= 1011 and mmdd <= 1130
      assign active_key = 'changeover'
    elsif mmdd >= 1201 and mmdd <= 1231
      assign active_key = 'deep_winter'
    elsif mmdd >= 101 and mmdd <= 310
      assign active_key = 'deep_winter'
    elsif mmdd >= 311 and mmdd <= 430
      assign active_key = 'spring'
    endif
  else
    assign active_key = mode
  endif

  assign active = null
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.season_key == active_key
      assign active = block
      break
    endif
  endfor
  unless active
    assign active = section.blocks.first
  endunless
  if active
    assign active_key = active.settings.season_key | default: active_key
  endif

  comment
    Season -> scene. Which road surface, which tire leads, whether it snows,
    and which brand colour lights the scene.
  endcomment
  assign road_season = 'summer'
  assign lead_tire = 'allterrain'
  assign snowy = false
  assign warm = true

  case active_key
    when 'preseason'
      assign road_season = 'summer'
      assign lead_tire = 'winter'
      assign snowy = true
      assign warm = false
    when 'changeover'
      assign road_season = 'winter'
      assign lead_tire = 'winter'
      assign snowy = true
      assign warm = false
    when 'deep_winter'
      assign road_season = 'winter'
      assign lead_tire = 'winter'
      assign snowy = true
      assign warm = false
    when 'spring'
      assign road_season = 'summer'
      assign lead_tire = 'allseason'
      assign snowy = false
      assign warm = true
    when 'summer'
      assign road_season = 'summer'
      assign lead_tire = 'allterrain'
      assign snowy = false
      assign warm = true
  endcase

  unless section.settings.enable_snow
    assign snowy = false
  endunless

  if road_season == 'winter' and section.settings.road_winter_image != blank
    assign road = section.settings.road_winter_image
  elsif road_season != 'winter' and section.settings.road_summer_image != blank
    assign road = section.settings.road_summer_image
  endif
  if road != blank
    assign road_url = road | image_url: width: 2400
  elsif road_season == 'winter'
    assign road_url = 'pt-cine-road-winter.png' | file_url
  else
    assign road_url = 'pt-cine-road-summer.png' | file_url
  endif

  comment
    Tire order: the season's tire takes the front-centre plane, the rest fill in
    behind it. Cut-outs the merchant has not supplied are skipped, so the scene
    never renders a broken image.
  endcomment
  assign order = 'winter,allweather,allseason,allterrain'
  case lead_tire
    when 'winter'
      assign order = 'winter,allweather,allseason,allterrain'
    when 'allseason'
      assign order = 'allseason,allweather,allterrain,winter'
    when 'allterrain'
      assign order = 'allterrain,allseason,allweather,winter'
  endcase
  assign order = order | split: ','

  assign tire_urls = ''
  for k in order
    assign pick = ''
    assign fb = ''
    if k == 'winter'
      assign pick = section.settings.tire_winter
      assign fb = 'pt-cine-tire-winter.png'
    elsif k == 'allweather'
      assign pick = section.settings.tire_allweather
      assign fb = 'pt-cine-tire-allweather.png'
    elsif k == 'allseason'
      assign pick = section.settings.tire_allseason
      assign fb = 'pt-cine-tire-allseason.png'
    elsif k == 'allterrain'
      assign pick = section.settings.tire_allterrain
      assign fb = 'pt-cine-tire-allterrain.png'
    endif
    if pick != blank
      assign u = pick | image_url: width: 1000
    else
      assign u = fb | file_url
    endif
    if u != blank
      assign tire_urls = tire_urls | append: u | append: '||'
    endif
  endfor
  assign tire_urls = tire_urls | split: '||'
  assign tire_max = section.settings.tire_count | default: 4
  if tire_urls.size < tire_max
    assign tire_max = tire_urls.size
  endif

  comment
    Backdrop plates — one is a still, two or three slowly crossfade.
  endcomment
  assign skies = ''
  if section.settings.sky_image != blank
    assign s1 = section.settings.sky_image | image_url: width: 2400
  else
    assign s1 = 'pt-cine-sky.png' | file_url
  endif
  if s1 != blank
    assign skies = skies | append: s1 | append: '||'
  endif
  if section.settings.sky_image_2 != blank
    assign s2 = section.settings.sky_image_2 | image_url: width: 2400
    assign skies = skies | append: s2 | append: '||'
  endif
  if section.settings.sky_image_3 != blank
    assign s3 = section.settings.sky_image_3 | image_url: width: 2400
    assign skies = skies | append: s3 | append: '||'
  endif
  assign skies = skies | split: '||'
-%}

{%- if active -%}
<section
  class="psp psp--{{ active_key }}{% if snowy %} psp--snowy{% endif %}{% if warm %} psp--warm{% endif %}{% if skies.size > 1 %} psp--rotating{% endif %}"
  data-pt-season="{{ active_key }}"
  style="
    --psp-tire-size: {{ section.settings.tire_front_size | default: 44 }}vh;
    --psp-tire-x: {{ section.settings.tire_spread | default: 34 }}%;
    --psp-lean: {{ section.settings.tire_lean | default: -7 }}deg;
    --psp-dim: {{ section.settings.dim | default: 55 | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --psp-sky-dur: {{ section.settings.sky_interval | default: 9 | times: skies.size | at_least: 9 }}s;
  "
  {{ active.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- comment -%} 0 — backdrop plate(s) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if skies.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="psp__sky" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- for s in skies -%}
        <img
          class="psp__sky-img"
          style="--i: {{ forloop.index0 }};"
          src="{{ s }}"
          alt=""
          width="2688" height="1152"
          loading="{% if forloop.first %}eager{% else %}lazy{% endif %}"
          {% if forloop.first %}fetchpriority="high"{% endif %}
          decoding="async"
        >
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 1 — far road plate {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if road_url != blank -%}
    <div class="psp__road psp__road--far" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="{{ road_url }}" alt="" width="2688" height="1152" loading="eager" decoding="async">
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 2 — snow, far plane {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if snowy -%}
    <div class="psp__snow psp__snow--far" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 3 — tire cut-out planes {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if tire_max > 0 -%}
    <div class="psp__tires" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- for i in (1..tire_max) -%}
        <div class="psp__tire psp__tire--{{ i }}">
          <img src="{{ tire_urls[forloop.index0] }}" alt="" width="1000" height="1000" loading="{% if forloop.first %}eager{% else %}lazy{% endif %}" decoding="async">
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 4 — snow, near plane (in front of the tires) {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if snowy -%}
    <div class="psp__snow psp__snow--near" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 5 — front road plate: puts the tires inside the scene {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if road_url != blank -%}
    <div class="psp__road psp__road--near" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="{{ road_url }}" alt="" width="2688" height="1152" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} 6/7/9 — scrim, glow, vignette {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="psp__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="psp__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="psp__vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {%- comment -%} 8 — content {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="psp__inner">
    <div class="psp__meta">
      {%- if active.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="psp__eyebrow">
          <span class="psp__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {{ active.settings.eyebrow | escape }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Live conditions. Hidden until pt-weather.js has a real reading, so the
        page never shows a placeholder temperature or a stale one.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.enable_live_weather -%}
        <p class="psp__wx" data-pt-weather hidden>
          <span class="psp__wx-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span data-pt-temp></span>
          <span class="psp__wx-sep" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="psp__wx-note" data-pt-condition hidden></span>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <h1 class="psp__headline">{{ active.settings.headline | escape }}</h1>

    {%- if active.settings.subhead != blank -%}
      <p class="psp__subhead">{{ active.settings.subhead | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
      <div class="psp__search">
        {% render 'pt-smart-search', accent: '#dc2626' %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="psp__actions">
      {%- if active.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        <a class="psp__cta psp__cta--primary" href="{{ active.settings.cta_url | default: '/collections/tires' }}">
          {{ active.settings.cta_label | escape }}
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if active.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}
        <a class="psp__cta psp__cta--ghost" href="{{ active.settings.cta2_url | default: '/pages/booking' }}">
          {{ active.settings.cta2_label | escape }}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{%- if section.settings.enable_live_weather -%}
  <script src="{{ 'pt-weather.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
.psp {
  --psp-red:    #DC2626;
  --psp-orange: #F5820B;
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  overflow: hidden;
  min-height: clamp(580px, 86vh, 860px);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  background: #050608;
  color: #fff;
  font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif;
}
.psp * { box-sizing: border-box; }

/* 0. Backdrop plate(s) — one image is a still; two or three crossfade on a long
   cycle: the motion the slideshow had, without swapping the message. */
.psp__sky { position: absolute; inset: -4% 0 0 0; z-index: 0; }
.psp__sky-img {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center 42%;
  display: block;
  transform: scale(1.04);
}
.psp--rotating .psp__sky-img {
  opacity: 0;
  animation: psp-sky var(--psp-sky-dur, 27s) ease-in-out infinite;
  animation-delay: calc(var(--i, 0) * (var(--psp-sky-dur, 27s) / 3));
}
.psp--rotating .psp__sky-img:first-child { opacity: 1; }
@keyframes psp-sky {
  0%, 26%   { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.04); }
  33%, 93%  { opacity: 0; }
  100%      { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1.09); }
}

/* 1 / 5. Road plates — the same plate drawn twice: once behind the tires, once
   cropped in front, so the tires sit IN the surface rather than on it. */
.psp__road { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; pointer-events: none; }
.psp__road img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
.psp__road--far  { bottom: 0; height: 62%; z-index: 1; opacity: 0.96; }
.psp__road--near {
  bottom: -2px;
  height: 17%;
  z-index: 5;
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, #000 58%);
          mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, #000 58%);
}
.psp__road--near img { object-position: center bottom; }

/* 3. Tire cut-out planes — each has its own x, y, scale, brightness and depth.
   All share one --psp-lean so the set reads as a row, not four stickers. */
.psp__tires { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 3; pointer-events: none; }
.psp__tire {
  position: absolute;
  left: var(--tx, 50%);
  top: var(--ty, 86%);
  width: var(--ts, 44vh);
  height: var(--ts, 44vh);
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--psp-lean, -7deg));
  filter: brightness(var(--tbright, 1)) drop-shadow(0 26px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55));
  opacity: 0;
  animation: psp-tire-in 1.1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) var(--tdelay, 0.4s) forwards;
}
.psp__tire img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; display: block; }
@keyframes psp-tire-in {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%, -38%) rotate(var(--psp-lean, -7deg)) scale(0.94); }
  to   { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--psp-lean, -7deg)) scale(1); }
}

/* Plane 1 leads: largest, brightest, furthest forward. 3 and 4 sit deeper and
   dimmer so the eye reads distance. */
.psp__tire--1 { --tx: calc(50% + var(--psp-tire-x, 34%) * 0.62); --ty: 82%; --ts: var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh);              --tbright: 1;    --tdelay: 0.35s; z-index: 4; }
.psp__tire--2 { --tx: calc(50% + var(--psp-tire-x, 34%) * 1.28); --ty: 86%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.88); --tbright: 0.9;  --tdelay: 0.5s;  z-index: 3; }
.psp__tire--3 { --tx: calc(50% + var(--psp-tire-x, 34%) * 0.14); --ty: 90%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.72); --tbright: 0.72; --tdelay: 0.65s; z-index: 2; }
.psp__tire--4 { --tx: calc(50% + var(--psp-tire-x, 34%) * 1.74); --ty: 92%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.64); --tbright: 0.6;  --tdelay: 0.8s;  z-index: 1; }

/* 2 / 4. Snow — two planes, pure CSS, no images and no requests. The far plane
   sits behind the tires and the near plane in front, so snow falls THROUGH the
   scene. Both intensify when pt-weather.js reports real snowfall. */
.psp__snow {
  position: absolute;
  inset: -25% 0 0 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  background-repeat: repeat;
  will-change: transform;
}
.psp__snow--far {
  z-index: 2;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 12% 10%, rgba(255,255,255,0.55) 50%, transparent 51%),
    radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 62% 34%, rgba(255,255,255,0.45) 50%, transparent 51%),
    radial-gradient(1px 1px   at 84% 12%, rgba(255,255,255,0.40) 50%, transparent 51%),
    radial-gradient(1px 1px   at 37% 68%, rgba(255,255,255,0.40) 50%, transparent 51%);
  background-size: 340px 340px;
  animation: psp-fall 22s linear infinite;
  opacity: 0.5;
}
.psp__snow--near {
  z-index: 4;
  background-image:
    radial-gradient(3px 3px     at 18% 44%, rgba(255,255,255,0.85) 50%, transparent 51%),
    radial-gradient(2.5px 2.5px at 88% 24%, rgba(255,255,255,0.75) 50%, transparent 51%),
    radial-gradient(2px 2px     at 52% 74%, rgba(255,255,255,0.70) 50%, transparent 51%);
  background-size: 420px 420px;
  animation: psp-fall 9s linear infinite;
  opacity: 0.45;
  filter: blur(0.4px);
}
@keyframes psp-fall {
  from { transform: translate3d(0, -25%, 0); }
  to   { transform: translate3d(-46px, 25%, 0); }
}
.psp.is-snowing .psp__snow--far  { animation-duration: 14s; opacity: 0.72; }
.psp.is-snowing .psp__snow--near { animation-duration: 6s;  opacity: 0.68; }

/* 6. Scrim — directional, so the artwork keeps its depth. */
.psp__scrim {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 6;
  pointer-events: none;
  background:
    linear-gradient(100deg,
      rgba(5,6,8,calc(0.96 * var(--psp-dim, 0.55) / 0.55)) 0%,
      rgba(5,6,8,calc(0.74 * var(--psp-dim, 0.55) / 0.55)) 32%,
      rgba(5,6,8,calc(0.26 * var(--psp-dim, 0.55) / 0.55)) 62%,
      rgba(5,6,8,0.10) 100%),
    linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(5,6,8,0.60) 0%, transparent 20%);
}

/* 7. Season glow. */
.psp__glow {
  position: absolute;
  z-index: 6;
  left: -12%;
  top: 14%;
  width: 62%;
  height: 72%;
  pointer-events: none;
  filter: blur(18px);
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(220,38,38,0.22) 0%, rgba(220,38,38,0.07) 42%, transparent 70%);
  animation: psp-glow 11s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}
.psp--warm .psp__glow {
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(245,130,11,0.22) 0%, rgba(245,130,11,0.07) 42%, transparent 70%);
}
@keyframes psp-glow {
  from { opacity: 0.85; transform: scale(0.97); }
  to   { opacity: 1;    transform: scale(1.05); }
}

/* 9. Vignette. */
.psp__vignette {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 7;
  pointer-events: none;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 170px 44px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55);
}

/* 8. Content. */
.psp__inner {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 8;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 1280px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 6rem 2.4rem;
}
.psp__meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
.psp__eyebrow,
.psp__wx {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0.5rem 1.05rem 0.5rem 0.85rem;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.10);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);
  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-size: 1.18rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: 0.07em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.94);
}
.psp__pulse {
  width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0;
  background: var(--psp-red);
  animation: psp-pulse 2.2s ease-out infinite;
}
@keyframes psp-pulse {
  0%   { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(220,38,38,0.65); }
  70%  { box-shadow: 0 0 0 9px rgba(220,38,38,0); }
  100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(220,38,38,0); }
}
/* The live pill reads cooler than the season pill so the two don't compete. */
.psp__wx { letter-spacing: 0.05em; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.86); }
.psp__wx-dot {
  width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0;
  background: #7dd3fc;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(125,211,252,0.8);
}
.psp.is-freezing .psp__wx-dot { background: #bae6fd; }
.psp__wx-sep { width: 1px; height: 11px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.28); }
.psp__wx-note { color: #bae6fd; }
.psp__wx-note[hidden] { display: none; }
/* No condition worth naming -> drop the separator too */
.psp__wx-sep:has(+ [hidden]) { display: none; }

.psp__headline {
  font-family: 'Barlow Condensed', sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 6.4vw, 6.6rem);
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 0.98;
  margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  max-width: 19ch;
  text-shadow: 0 2px 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
}
.psp__subhead {
  font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 1.9vw, 1.85rem);
  font-weight: 300;
  line-height: 1.5;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.86);
  margin: 0 0 2.2rem;
  max-width: 52ch;
  text-shadow: 0 1px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
}
.psp__search { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.psp__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 2.6rem; }
.psp__cta {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.6rem;
  height: 52px;
  padding: 0 1.9rem;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 1.32rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: #fff;
  transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease, background 0.18s ease;
}
.psp__cta--primary {
  background: var(--psp-red);
  box-shadow: 0 10px 30px -10px rgba(220,38,38,0.75);
}
.psp__cta--primary:hover { background: #b91c1c; transform: translateY(-2px); }
.psp__cta--primary svg { transition: transform 0.18s ease; }
.psp__cta--primary:hover svg { transform: translateX(3px); }
.psp__cta--ghost {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.26);
  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
}
.psp__cta--ghost:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.16); transform: translateY(-2px); }
.psp__cta:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #fff; outline-offset: 3px; }

/* Responsive. */
@media (max-width: 989px) {
  .psp { min-height: clamp(560px, 80svh, 760px); }
  .psp__inner { padding: 4.5rem 2rem; }
  .psp__headline { max-width: 15ch; }
  .psp__scrim {
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(5,6,8,0.94) 0%, rgba(5,6,8,0.68) 46%, rgba(5,6,8,0.34) 100%);
  }
  /* Tires drop to a shallower row along the bottom so the copy keeps the top */
  .psp__tire--1 { --tx: 74%; --ty: 90%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.68); }
  .psp__tire--2 { --tx: 96%; --ty: 93%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.58); }
  .psp__tire--3 { --tx: 52%; --ty: 95%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.48); }
  .psp__tire--4 { display: none; }
  .psp__road--far { height: 46%; }
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .psp { min-height: auto; }
  .psp__inner { padding: 3.6rem 1.6rem 3rem; }
  .psp__headline { font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 10.5vw, 4rem); max-width: 13ch; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .psp__subhead { font-size: 1.35rem; margin-bottom: 1.8rem; max-width: 40ch; }
  .psp__eyebrow, .psp__wx { font-size: 1.02rem; padding: 0.42rem 0.9rem 0.42rem 0.75rem; }
  .psp__actions { gap: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .psp__cta { height: 48px; font-size: 1.22rem; flex: 1 1 100%; justify-content: center; }
  .psp__tire--1 { --tx: 78%; --ty: 94%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.56); }
  .psp__tire--2 { --tx: 100%; --ty: 97%; --ts: calc(var(--psp-tire-size, 44vh) * 0.46); }
  .psp__tire--3 { display: none; }
  .psp__vignette { box-shadow: inset 0 0 100px 26px rgba(0,0,0,0.5); }
  .psp__snow--far { opacity: 0.4; }
}

/* Motion sensitivity. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .psp__sky-img,
  .psp__snow,
  .psp__glow,
  .psp__pulse { animation: none !important; }
  .psp--rotating .psp__sky-img { opacity: 0; }
  .psp--rotating .psp__sky-img:first-child { opacity: 1; }
  .psp__tire { animation: none; opacity: 1; }
  .psp__snow { opacity: 0.25; }
  .psp__cta { transition: none; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

